INT. HYDROPONIC GARDEN DECK - STARSHIP VESPERIA - DAY

Tiers of green racks under purple grow-lamps. Mist drifts. Beyond a long window, stars wheel slowly.

COMMANDER YUSUF ADEBAYO-LIND, 50s, tall, silver beard, in a gray flight suit, trims a tomato vine. BOTANIST IXCHEL MORALES, 30s, small and wiry, scribbles notes. A cleaning drone named SCRUB, 2 feet tall, hums along the floor. ENSIGN BRODERICK PELL, 20s, freckled, carries a tray of seedlings. A maintenance tech, KOFI AMOAH-REYES, 40s, hangs upside down in a service hatch.

Pell trips over Scrub. The tray flies. Ixchel dives to catch it. Kofi drops a wrench. Yusuf catches the wrench. Scrub spins in a circle and chirps.

ENSIGN PELL
Sorry, sir.

COMMANDER YUSUF
It's a garden, Ensign. Things fall.

Ixchel sets the tray down on a rack. Kofi swings out of the hatch and lands upright.

KOFI
Irrigation's back online.

IXCHEL
Finally.

They all stand a moment, watching the mist settle on the leaves.
